Start with an unvisited point in the dataset.

Mark it as visited.

Find all points within ε distance (neighborhood).

If the number of points in the neighborhood is greater than or equal to MinPts,

Mark the point as a core point.

Create a new cluster.

Expand the cluster by visiting all neighbors recursively.

If the number of neighbors is less than MinPts,

Mark it as a noise point.

It may later be included in a cluster if it falls within the neighborhood of a core point.

Repeat the process until all points are visited.